From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baptiste Augrain <daiyam@zokugun.org>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: report issues against the vscodium repository instead of
 microsoft/vscode

VSCodium ships as its own distribution, so the issue reporter, the slow-extension report, and the guidance wiki link must file against the VSCodium GitHub repo rather than microsoft/vscode, and the "VS Code" source labels are rebranded to the product name. The Microsoft-internal duplicate-candidates service (vscode-probot) is unreachable here, so duplicate detection falls back to searching GitHub issues in the same repo (#825).

